1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:14,330
X six is the Symmedian Point— also known as the Lemoine Point or Grebe Point: the concurrence of the three symmedians obtained by reflecting each median across its corresponding interior angle bisector, and the perspector of the tangential triangle.

2
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:28,680
Its trilinear distances are directly proportional to the side lengths, a, to b, to c, which makes X six the unique point inside triangle A B C that minimizes the sum of the squares of the perpendicular distances to the three sidelines.

3
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:35,733
Its barycentric sub-triangle areas are proportional to the squares of the sides, a squared, to b squared, to c squared.

4
00:00:35,733 --> 00:00:41,720
On the central lines layer, X six anchors the Brocard axis through X three, X fifteen, and X sixteen.

5
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:52,260
X six is the isogonal conjugate of the Centroid X two, the isotomic conjugate of the third Brocard point X seventy-six, and the Gergonne point of the tangential triangle.
